            "id": "1",
            "text": "**Red flags**  \n- Major drug\u2011drug interaction between warfarin and amiodarone \u2192 risk of supratherapeutic INR and serious bleeding.  \n- Any unexpected rise in INR >\u202f4.0 warrants immediate action (hold warfarin, consider vitamin\u202fK).  \n\n**What to do now (stabilising measure)**  \n- Obtain a baseline INR before starting amiodarone.  \n- Reduce the warfarin dose by roughly 30\u201150\u202f%\u202fat the time amiodarone is initiated.  \n- Re\u2011check INR in 2\u20113\u202fdays, then weekly until stable.  \n\n**Bottom line** \u2013 It\u2019s not \u201csafe\u201d to add amiodarone without adjusting the warfarin dose and close INR monitoring.  \n\nSynthetic teaching case - not medical advice.",
            "response_type": "text"
          }
        ],
